WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.560
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.530
The
Wasp's
Nest

Pirate
Island

12
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.550
Hey, ya hear that?

13
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:39.560
If the world sank into the sea
a long time ago, wouldn’t that mean...

14
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.400
there’s treasure scattered
on the sea floor all over the world?!

15
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.150
You dumbass! That don’t mean
the entire world was a City of Gold!

16
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.820
Still! There’s gotta be some treasure
down there, for sure!

17
00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.410
Use your head! Even if there is,
it’s 200 meters under water!

18
00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.040
How d’ya even go that deep?!

19
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.330
We’d be gobbled up whole
by Sea Beasts.

20
00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.550
Well, I hear tell there’s ships out there
that can dive deep into the ocean.

21
00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:14.800
Sure, and ya think we have
the means to buy one?! Hell no!

22
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.010
Yeah, I guess it’d be easier
just to make friends with a Mermaid!

23
00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.230
Mermaids! I’d love to meet one!

24
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.710
Grand
Line

25
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:29.880
Long before the time of Noland,

26
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:35.380
Saruyama Alliance Pirates - Last Boss
Montblanc Cricket

27
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.780
a kingdom with an advanced civilization

28
00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.380
sank into the sea, huh?

29
00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.290
Helluva story!

30
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.100
Masira, Shojo!

31
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.540
Wanna go diving again?

32
00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.210
Now, this is what dreams are made of!

33
00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.440
We’d follow you anywhere, Pops!

34
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.300
New
World

35
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.760
Ring, ring, ring...

36
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.360
Clik.

37
00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.570
Tashigi.

38
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.280
Smoker.

39
00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.370
Where are you now?

40
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.660
I’m at GS General Hospital.

41
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.060
Marine
GS General
Hospital

42
00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.080
Koby...

43
00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.570
So that means the One Piece is...

44
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.530
Yeah, this is a lot to take in...

45
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.760
I’m feeling lightheaded.

46
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.510
I’d better write it down later
to try and sort it out...

47
00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.220
My brain can’t keep up.

48
00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.390
Focus on healing up first.

49
00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.480
Get involved now,
and you’ll just hold the rest of us back.

50
00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.490
How’d it go?

51
00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.950
The Captain’s making
a good recovery as well.

52
00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.910
Good to hear.

53
00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.580
But he wanted to be alone.

54
00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.540
I see...

55
00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.880
Prince...

56
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.590
If what Vegapunk is saying is true,

57
00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.380
wouldn’t this lead to a grave conclusion?

58
00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.510
It would.

59
00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.140
Looks like this’ll lead
to some seriously awful answers.

60
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.680
In that case...

61
00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.580
it’s time for us, SWORD, to step in!

62
00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.670
Marine HQ Special Ops
SWORD Captain
X Drake

63
00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.690
I know that my information is fragmented,

64
00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:41.610
but providing the complete story
 would require me to add speculation.

65
00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.240
Just tell us!

66
00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.310
What did Roger leave behind after
learning all about the Void Century, then?!

67
00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:52.290
Labophase

Egghead

68
00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.170
Look! The barrier’s been deactivated!

69
00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:01.380
Ooh! Now we can get the hell outta here!

70
00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.850
Now, what was that crash we heard earlier?
Scared the crap outta me!

71
00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.310
Seems like the clouds stopped stretching.

72
00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:12.520
It’s long enough now.
I think we can reach the sea.

73
00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.730
But...

74
00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.860
looks like a ton of ships have gathered
around our splashdown point.

75
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.260
Cola barrels in place!

76
00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.480
You can eject anytime!

77
00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.080
Okay!

78
00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.790
Jinbe, not here yet?!

79
00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.460
We’re almost there, but...

80
00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.420
right now...

81
00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.800
we’re following some kind of
mystery monster!

82
00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.340
What?!

83
00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.430
Hey, what’s with the detour?!
Come straight here—

84
00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.140
This is no detour!

85
00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.730
The monster’s coming your way!
Watch out!

86
00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:57.800
Huh?!

87
00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.530
A truly overwhelming presence
it’s got, indeed!

88
00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:12.480
The Five Elders?!

89
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.980
Whaaa?!

90
00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.040
Jinbe!

91
00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.000
Got ya!

92
00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.490
Fishman Jujutsu:

93
00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.160
Piggyback!

94
00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.970
Two-Sword Style:

95
00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.560
Restful Paradise...

96
00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.810
Rashomon!

97
00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.290
– Kitetsu?!
– Kitetsu?!

98
00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.300
Whoa!

99
00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.470
Zoro!

100
00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:12.930
Get the ship moving!

101
00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:14.890
We’ll just hop on!

102
00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.690
Do it now,
while you got the chance!

103
00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:20.840
North-
Eastern
coast

Egghead

104
00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.010
Straw Hat! You’re still not here?!

105
00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.950
Hurry! Even this ship
can’t hold out against this!

106
00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.580
It’s just one ship!

107
00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.440
Forget the legends!

108
00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:39.250
Send that ancient Elbaph ship
to the bottom of the ocean!

109
00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.840
How long are you gonna
keep us waiting, Luffy?!

110
00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.720
He’s out of our signal range, isn’t he?

111
00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:59.520
Luffy!

112
00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.550
Yeah!

113
00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.860
We’re almost there! Get the ship moving!

114
00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.740
I can’t believe shouting worked...

115
00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.990
Get over here already!

116
00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:18.730
Yeah! We’ll be there soon!

117
00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.590
That’s our ship!

118
00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:25.170
Woohoo!
Can’t wait to climb aboard!

119
00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.630
Oimo, Kashi!

120
00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.010
That’s...

121
00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.580
The Captains!

122
00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.390
Get the ship moving!

123
00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.730
You got it, Captain!

124
00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.270
Set sail!

125
00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.230
Turn her about!

126
00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.540
Don’t let them get away!

127
00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.530
Don’t back down!

128
00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.580
They’re just some pirate fossils
from a hundred years ago!

129
00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.460
Shake ‘em off our tail...

130
00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.460
ye boys!

131
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:05.630
Hey! Don’t give up! Keep fighting!

132
00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.610
We can’t handle them!

133
00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.530
Abandon posts!
All ships, form up on me!

134
00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.520
I want an all-out assault!

135
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.640
Just pathetic!

136
00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.250
Ain’t y’all gonna make
a stand for justice?!

137
00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:29.360
Act like the heroes you are,
not a bunch of scrubs!

138
00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:41.390
Vice Admiral Bluegrass!

139
00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.350
Whoa! That put a hole in the ship!

140
00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.800
I’ll put one in you too!

141
00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.430
Rock-n-Roll...

142
00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.180
Blaster!

143
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.590
Whoa! Vice Admiral Doll!

144
00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.410
Love a good brawler!

145
00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.370
Kashi!

146
00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:24.890
Keep it up! So what
if they’re giants?!

147
00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:38.180
Huh?

148
00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:41.140
That boar ain’t after us no more!

149
00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.060
Where’d it go?

150
00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:49.190
That’s a good thing! Means all we
gotta do now is hop on the ship and...

151
00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:52.150
Yup! And sail away!

152
00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.140
In closing,

153
00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.810
I want to deliver a single message:

154
00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.360
Look! That must be...

155
00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:21.240
Yes... The very same iron giant...

156
00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:25.240
that attacked Mary Geoise
200 years ago.

157
00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:33.320
There is no mistaking it!

158
00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.280
To those scattered across the world...

159
00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:40.090
...who bear the name of “D”!

160
00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.750
Ace... Luffy...

161
00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.520
Luffy... Vice Admiral Garp!

162
00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.270
Captain!

163
00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.050
Damn you!

164
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.640
Within each and every one of you...

165
00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:13.750
lies—

166
00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.370
That is quite enough out of you...

167
00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.150
Vegapunk!

168
00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.860
It cut out!

169
00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:47.160
What was he going to say?!

170
00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.270
What did he mean by “D”?!

171
00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.980
Signal jamming?
Right at the crucial moment, too!

172
00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.190
Damn it all!

173
00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.550
It stopped...

174
00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.180
Abandon ship!

175
00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.810
What the hell’s with
that iron monster?!

176
00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.520
The ship’s gonna go under!

177
00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:26.110
that name...

178
00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.900
Where are you?

179
00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.960
Joyboy...

180
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.860
Where did you go?

181
00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.130
I want to see you...

182
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.600
You were just here, right?

183
00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.190
Joyboy...

184
00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:00.820
That’s strange...

185
00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.780
So very strange...

186
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:11.720
<b>The Most Free</b>

187
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.040
Technical issues?

188
00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.150
He was still talking!

189
00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:21.690
What could have caused
the transmission to stop?

190
00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:24.800
And why did Vegapunk die
in the first place?

191
00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.800
Someone assassinated him, maybe?

192
00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.970
He said he’d committed crimes...

193
00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.640
Maybe he was taken out
by the World Government?

194
00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:36.750
Well, Straw Hat Luffy was
holding him hostage in the first place!

195
00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.600
He’s a pirate!
He’s got to be the one to blame!

196
00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.560
No matter what crimes
he committed,

197
00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:45.050
there’s no way the Government
would kill the world’s greatest genius!

198
00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:48.030
Den it must’ve been Luffyland...

199
00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:49.990
Not a chance!

200
00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.060
What the hell is that?!

201
00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.910
A boar?! Or a mammoth?!

202
00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.280
Wha?!

203
00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:10.450
What’s going on in Egghead?!

204
00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.680
York.

205
00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.140
York!

206
00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.960
Huh? What is it?

207
00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:21.810
How many of the Vegapunks
 are still alive?

208
00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.940
The Vegapunks... Me and...

209
00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.780
The number of people
accessing Punk Records right now...

210
00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.140
is two!

211
00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.870
Lilith is on this floor!

212
00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:37.290
And Atlas is on the northeast coast!

213
00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.660
Well done.

214
00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.750
Shall we erase them all?

215
00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:42.960
Yes.

216
00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.610
Even after Stella’s death,

217
00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:50.300
Punk Records was designed
to continue growing.

218
00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.580
York’s development is beneficial for us,

219
00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:57.470
but we have no need for other geniuses!

220
00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.310
Go on, Stussy.

221
00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:07.550
You “know full well what I’ll do next”, right?

222
00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:09.990
We were friends?

223
00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.030
Don’t make me laugh.

224
00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:17.830
If anything, I respected you
as a ruthless colleague.

225
00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.900
But once Lucci gets here,
I won’t be able to stop him!

226
00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.570
Hey, Kaku. I...

227
00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:27.610
Go!

228
00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.380
Set sail!

229
00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:49.980
We’re gettin’ outta here!

230
00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:52.150
Aye!

231
00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:56.470
All right! Hop aboard!

232
00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.120
Yeaaah!

233
00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.750
It’s the Captains!

234
00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.210
Here he comes.

235
00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.490
Luffy!

236
00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.840
You’re all right!

237
00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.510
O’ course we are!

238
00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.470
It’s the Giants’ ship!

239
00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.840
It’s so huge!

240
00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:31.860
Isn’t Usopp here yet?
What about Chopper?

241
00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:33.860
Nope, they’re still up there.

242
00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:35.570
Thanks for bringin’ Luffy!

243
00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:39.030
Got your ass kicked, huh, Kashi?

244
00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:45.750
Oimo, Kashi!

245
00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.330
Straw Hat!

246
00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.860
Good to see you, man!

247
00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:53.130
Yeah! Hey, got somethin’ to eat?

248
00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.140
Dammit... After ‘em!

249
00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.560
Don’t let ‘em get away!

250
00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:07.980
We’ve plenty o’ warships!

251
00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.190
The Giants are too powerful...!

252
00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:13.730
Are you okay?!

253
00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.650
Vice Admiral Doll!

254
00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:18.890
Vice Admiral Bluegrass!

255
00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.700
I hate being so powerless...

256
00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.790
That’s some ability!

257
00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.370
Damn you, Bonney!

258
00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:29.110
You’ll be in real big trouble
if you let me get away, right, Marines?

259
00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:32.280
Fire!

260
00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:37.130
Sanji here, we just set sail.

261
00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.010
Nami, how’s things up there?

262
00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.580
We’re about to leave, too!

263
00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:43.810
Thanks to Edison,
we should be able to reach the sea,

264
00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:47.600
but please try to help us
if it looks like we won’t reach the water!

265
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.210
Nooo!

266
00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.810
Of course!

267
00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:53.300
Nami, Robin, Lilith...

268
00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.740
I’ll rescue you,
even if all the other guys drown!

269
00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.110
Rescue everyone!

270
00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.990
I'll keep the ship safe!

271
00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:01.640
Save us with it!

272
00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.830
Something’s coming
from the center of the island!

273
00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:12.040
It figures they wouldn’t give up yet...

274
00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.790
The Five Elders.

275
00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:20.950
Oh! My, now... You must be
Straw Hat Luffy, then?

276
00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:27.060
The Captains did tell me to prepare
a lot of food because you’re a big eater.

277
00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.310
I was gonna serve this
to you guys later.

278
00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.100
Sorry!

279
00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.190
I need dis now.
Can you make ‘nother one o’ dese?

280
00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:38.510
You sure got a big appetite!

281
00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.350
Dammit, he’s gonna catch up to us!

282
00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:46.560
We gotta fight!

283
00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.840
Protect the puny humans!

284
00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.420
That’s hot!

285
00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.660
Are you okay, Bjørn, Sig?!

286
00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.300
You saved us! We owe you one!

287
00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.620
Put out the fire!

288
00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:06.640
Keep the fire away from the sails!

289
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:10.730
I wanna get Daddy and Vegapunk
somewhere else! We’ll be roasted alive here!

290
00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:11.850
Let me...!

291
00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:16.020
Guess we really can’t just
ignore those monsters.

292
00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:20.440
Not when one of ‘em can fly!
It’ll follow us anywhere we go!

293
00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:23.860
Here comes another one!

294
00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.330
There’s that sound again...

295
00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:40.210
All right! I’m full!

296
00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.920
We’re countin’ on you, Luffy!

297
00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:57.130
Uh?! Is this what he was
just talking about?

298
00:21:57.130 --> 00:22:00.030
The sea level’s already rising?!

299
00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.110
Holy crap!

300
00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.870
Here we go!

301
00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.370
Let the rhythm move you!

302
00:22:30.850 --> 00:22:33.730
Hey! It’s a festival rhythm!

303
00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:43.690
You idiot, quit dancing
and put out the fire!

304
00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:45.360
Same to you!

305
00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.100
Bonney!

306
00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:14.270
Bonney!

307
00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:18.020
Nika?!

308
00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.980
Like I keep askin’, who’s that?

309
00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:23.980
Let’s go. You wanna beat those
guys up, don’t you?

310
00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:26.280
That’s impossible for me!

311
00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:28.140
‘Cause I’m not like you...

312
00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:30.200
You can do it!

313
00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.910
Don’t got a clue how
your ability works, though!

314
00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:39.420
That’s just how I look when I’m free!

315
00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:52.720
What’s that?!

316
00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.270
Distortion Future!

317
00:23:57.940 --> 00:23:59.690
Future Where...

318
00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:02.690
...I’m the Most Free!

319
00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.150
Now you’re gettin’ it, Bonney!

320
00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.870
Don’t worry, Ginny...

321
00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:21.790
I’ll raise your daughter.

322
00:24:26.590 --> 00:24:27.630
I did it!

323
00:24:27.630 --> 00:24:29.220
Yeah!

324
00:24:31.840 --> 00:24:33.620
There’s two Nikas!

325
00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:35.510
Who are they?!

326
00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:37.710
White Giants?!

327
00:24:39.940 --> 00:24:41.380
I sense a peculiar presence...

328
00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:43.340
Let us hurry.

329
00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:49.360
Let’s go!

330
00:24:51.320 --> 00:24:52.110
Yeah!

331
00:25:04.500 --> 00:25:05.710
There...!

332
00:25:14.180 --> 00:25:16.080
Now things’re gettin’ fun!

333
00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:19.890
That’s the face on
Straw Hat Luffy’s wanted poster!

334
00:25:19.890 --> 00:25:21.640
Nika!

335
00:25:22.100 --> 00:25:24.230
Two Nikas?

336
00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:26.840
A mere illusion,
created by the Age-Age Fruit!

337
00:25:26.840 --> 00:25:29.170
Do not tempt fate!

338
00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:39.370
Luffy! Stop that Elder!

339
00:25:40.870 --> 00:25:42.330
I got this!

340
00:25:42.330 --> 00:25:44.040
Nika!

341
00:25:45.380 --> 00:25:46.500
Listen up, boys!

342
00:25:46.500 --> 00:25:49.990
Shreddin’ ‘em or crushin’ ‘em
won’t do nothin’ to ‘em!

343
00:25:59.770 --> 00:26:02.140
Huh?! So what’re you doing, then?!

344
00:26:05.730 --> 00:26:07.340
So...

345
00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:12.070
I want you all to hit me
as hard as you can!

346
00:26:14.320 --> 00:26:16.990
You’re telling me the only option’s
to send them flying?!

347
00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:19.740
Got it! As hard as I can, right?!

348
00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:23.290
What?! We’re gonna hit Luffy?!

349
00:26:23.290 --> 00:26:24.370
Why?!

350
00:26:24.370 --> 00:26:29.000
We’re counting on you, guys!
Take care of the bird!

351
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:33.130
Put out the fire and get us sailin’ again!
And quit dancing, you morons!

352
00:26:33.130 --> 00:26:34.510
Huh?!

353
00:26:34.510 --> 00:26:36.410
But you were doing it too!

354
00:26:48.060 --> 00:26:50.440
What are you doing?! Release me!

355
00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:52.900
Hurry up!

356
00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:55.850
What?!

357
00:26:55.850 --> 00:26:57.390
You’re really gonna hit him?!

358
00:26:57.390 --> 00:27:00.600
Captain’s orders, Bonney!

359
00:27:01.370 --> 00:27:03.830
Ifrit Jambe:

360
00:27:04.750 --> 00:27:07.330
Strong Impact...

361
00:27:11.210 --> 00:27:13.740
Don’t keep wafflin’ about it, Bonney!

362
00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:17.410
Hit me as hard as you can!

363
00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:19.640
All right then...

364
00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:21.010
Super-Size...

365
00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:25.100
Hell Memories!

366
00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:27.560
Right!

367
00:27:27.940 --> 00:27:30.940
Nika Punch!

368
00:27:39.490 --> 00:27:40.990
That hurts!

369
00:27:40.990 --> 00:27:44.240
What?! We’re hurting you?!

370
00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:51.860
Of course you are...

371
00:27:51.860 --> 00:27:55.460
because y’all are using Haki!

372
00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:01.800
Gum-Gum...

373
00:28:02.300 --> 00:28:04.720
Don’t lose your grip, Bonney!

374
00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:07.680
Push hard, like yer tryin’
to squeeze the life outta him!

375
00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:09.920
What is up with you guys?!

376
00:28:14.820 --> 00:28:15.900
Dawn...

377
00:28:15.900 --> 00:28:17.360
Balloon!

378
00:28:26.830 --> 00:28:28.540
All right, away it goes!

379
00:28:29.210 --> 00:28:31.400
And it ain’t never comin’ back!

380
00:28:33.650 --> 00:28:35.280
We did it!

381
00:28:37.260 --> 00:28:39.630
Let’s get goin’, people!

382
00:28:43.720 --> 00:28:45.580
So, where’s Usopp and the others?

383
00:28:46.080 --> 00:28:48.790
They were supposed to be
on their way down by now...

384
00:28:48.790 --> 00:28:50.060
They’re takin’ forever...

385
00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:53.770
Something might’ve happened up there.

386
00:28:53.770 --> 00:28:56.230
Huh? Atlas...

387
00:28:57.610 --> 00:28:58.940
I’ll go check!

388
00:28:58.940 --> 00:29:01.150
Wait, Atlas!

389
00:29:01.150 --> 00:29:04.530
York is monitoring both of us...

390
00:29:04.530 --> 00:29:07.160
Lilith, we’re...

391
00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:12.620
...nothing...

392
00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:16.530
...nothing...

393
00:29:16.530 --> 00:29:18.000
It’s back!

394
00:29:18.420 --> 00:29:20.670
What?! It’s back on!

395
00:29:20.670 --> 00:29:23.720
...inherited through the generations...

396
00:29:24.340 --> 00:29:25.760
...can be called a will...

397
00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:27.720
What’s he talking about?

398
00:29:28.140 --> 00:29:31.460
It came back on!
Was it just bad reception?

399
00:29:32.190 --> 00:29:34.770
So you just cut off
the Mental Waves temporarily!

400
00:29:35.190 --> 00:29:39.360
A Transmission Transponder Snail’s memory
and Mental Waves’re on separate circuits!

401
00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:42.400
Yous gotta destroy
the actual thing, Elders!

402
00:29:42.780 --> 00:29:45.530
I pray this message will surely find...

403
00:29:45.530 --> 00:29:50.290
those at the mercy of this reason.

404
00:29:55.540 --> 00:29:57.250
Guh?! Why?!

405
00:30:03.220 --> 00:30:05.550
Rain? A bombardment?!

406
00:30:05.550 --> 00:30:06.410
No!

407
00:30:07.890 --> 00:30:10.720
It’s a bunch of rubble
and Cipher Pol agents!

408
00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:12.430
Why are they falling from the sky?!

409
00:30:12.430 --> 00:30:15.380
Catch them! Or they’re gonna die!

410
00:30:17.770 --> 00:30:19.840
Seraphim are with them, too!

411
00:30:23.260 --> 00:30:26.950
Hey, old guy! That monster’s
the one spittin’ them out!

412
00:30:28.240 --> 00:30:29.740
Looks like a fountain!

413
00:30:29.740 --> 00:30:33.370
It’s gonna come this way!
Hurry up and get away from it!

414
00:30:43.170 --> 00:30:45.260
Huh, this again?!

415
00:30:45.260 --> 00:30:46.840
Here it comes!

416
00:30:46.840 --> 00:30:49.010
It’s inhalin’ us! Get us outta here!

417
00:30:49.930 --> 00:30:52.750
We’re bein’ pulled back!

418
00:31:02.610 --> 00:31:04.780
I can’t keep going...

419
00:31:04.780 --> 00:31:06.860
Freedom’s exhausting...

420
00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:10.780
Bonney?!

421
00:31:12.790 --> 00:31:16.040
Furl the sails! Use the oars!

422
00:31:20.750 --> 00:31:22.530
Ya big jerk...!

423
00:31:22.960 --> 00:31:25.220
Naptime for you, pal!

424
00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:34.100
Get ‘em, Nika!

425
00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:36.870
White Giants! Monsters!

426
00:31:36.870 --> 00:31:41.310
Cipher Pol falling from the sky!
Have I been dreaming the whole time?!

427
00:31:48.430 --> 00:31:50.200
Oh, crap!

428
00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:52.560
The boar’s headed your way!
Watch out!

429
00:31:52.560 --> 00:31:55.270
That thing’s super tough!

430
00:31:55.270 --> 00:31:57.080
Not that one!

431
00:31:57.080 --> 00:32:00.500
He’ll smash the ship to pieces!
We gotta flee!

432
00:32:13.390 --> 00:32:15.220
Joyboy!

433
00:32:48.550 --> 00:32:50.170
Got that, Emet?

434
00:32:50.840 --> 00:32:52.390
Only when the time is right.

435
00:33:00.230 --> 00:33:02.130
Time is right?

436
00:33:02.130 --> 00:33:05.610
What the hell is that?!

437
00:33:17.770 --> 00:33:20.560
Robooo!

438
00:33:31.030 --> 00:33:35.250
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

439
00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:39.470
